   "source": [
    "### Duplicate and Split Leakage Review\n",
    "\n",
    "A small number of duplicate records remain within the processed training and validation datasets. Because the datasets were created using a random stratified split, an additional check is performed to determine whether identical feature records appear in both the training and validation sets.\n",
    "\n",
    "Cross-split duplicates may introduce data leakage because the model could be evaluated on observations identical to records it encountered during training."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "8a65b8bf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Unique training feature rows: 1764095\n",
      "Unique validation feature rows: 378094\n",
      "Identical feature rows across train and validation: 190\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Create unique feature-only records for the overlap check\n",
    "train_unique = X_train.drop_duplicates()\n",
    "val_unique = X_val.drop_duplicates()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Find identical feature rows appearing in both datasets\n",
    "overlap = train_unique.merge(\n",
    "    val_unique,\n",
    "    how=\"inner\",\n",
    "    on=X_train.columns.tolist()\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Unique training feature rows:\", len(train_unique))\n",
    "print(\"Unique validation feature rows:\", len(val_unique))\n",
    "print(\"Identical feature rows across train and validation:\", len(overlap))"
   ]
  },
